%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 763b7bf307cb4ee4e8fa0a2befef6ddb, type: 3}
  m_Name: ReviewLibrary
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CircuitCrafter.Guidance.ReviewLibrary
  rules:
  - ruleName: Cooler still mounted
    moduleId: 
    category: 
    keywords:
    - heatsink is still mounted
    whatWentWrong: The CPU cooler is still mounted on top.
    howToFix: Remove the heatsink and fan first.
    correctProcedure: Unplug the CPU fan cable, release the cooler's clips or screws
      evenly, and lift the cooler off. Only then open the socket lever and load plate
      and lift the CPU straight out by its edges.
    areaToImprove: CPU handling
    activityId: coc1-disassembly
  - ruleName: CPU not secured for cooler
    moduleId: 
    category: 
    keywords:
    - load plate is still open
    - retention lever is still open
    - cpu is not installed
    whatWentWrong: The CPU isn't secured yet.
    howToFix: Seat the CPU, close the load plate and lower the lever - then fit the
      cooler.
    correctProcedure: Seat the CPU (gold triangle to the socket mark), close the
      load plate, lower and latch the retention lever, apply thermal paste if the
      cooler has none, then fit the cooler and plug its fan into CPU_FAN.
    areaToImprove: CPU handling
    activityId: coc1-assembly
  - ruleName: CPU socket locked
    moduleId: 
    category: 
    keywords:
    - cpu lock is still closed
    - case lock is still closed
    - open the main cpu lock
    whatWentWrong: The CPU socket is still locked.
    howToFix: Lift the socket lever and open the load plate first.
    correctProcedure: 'To remove: lift the retention lever, open the load plate,
      and lift the CPU straight up by its edges. To install: line up the gold triangle
      with the socket mark, lower the CPU in without pressing, close the load plate
      and lever, then fit the cooler with fresh thermal paste.'
    areaToImprove: CPU handling
    activityId: coc1-assembly
  - ruleName: Removal out of order
    moduleId: 
    category: 
    keywords:
    - must come off first
    whatWentWrong: That part can't come off yet - something is still in the way.
    howToFix: Remove the parts on top of it first.
    correctProcedure: 'Disassemble from the outside in: 1) shut down, unplug and
      wear the ESD strap; 2) remove the side panel; 3) disconnect power and data
      cables; 4) remove expansion cards and RAM; 5) remove the CPU cooler, then the
      CPU; 6) remove the drives and the power supply; 7) remove the motherboard last.
      Reassemble in the reverse order.'
    areaToImprove: Component removal sequence
    activityId: coc1-disassembly
  - ruleName: Cable still connected
    moduleId: 
    category: 
    keywords:
    - plugged in
    whatWentWrong: A cable is still connected to that part.
    howToFix: Unplug its cable first - hold the connector, not the wire.
    correctProcedure: Before removing a component, disconnect every power and data
      cable attached to it. Grip the connector body, press any locking tab, and pull
      straight out. Never pull a cable by its wires.
    areaToImprove: Cable handling
    activityId: coc1-disassembly
  - ruleName: RAM clips closed
    moduleId: 
    category: 
    keywords:
    - still closed
    - clip
    whatWentWrong: The RAM retention clips are still closed.
    howToFix: Push both clips outward, then lift the module straight up.
    correctProcedure: 'Open both retention clips and lift the module straight out,
      holding it by the edges (never the gold contacts). To install: line up the
      notch with the key in the slot and press down evenly on both ends until the
      clips snap shut.'
    areaToImprove: Memory installation
    activityId: coc1-assembly
  - ruleName: Socket not ready
    moduleId: 
    category: 
    keywords:
    - tried to install '
    whatWentWrong: That socket isn't ready for the part.
    howToFix: Open the socket's clips or lever and check which way round it goes.
    correctProcedure: Prepare the slot or socket first (open clips or lever), match
      the part's notch or key to the socket, then seat it without forcing. A part
      that needs force is in the wrong way or the wrong socket.
    areaToImprove: Component installation
    activityId: coc1-assembly
  - ruleName: Partition not prepared
    moduleId: COC1
    category: 
    keywords:
    - partition
    - unallocated
    whatWentWrong: Windows can't be installed to that space yet.
    howToFix: Select the unallocated space, click New, then Apply.
    correctProcedure: 'In Windows Setup choose Custom: Install Windows only. Select
      the unallocated space and click New > Apply - Setup creates its system partitions.
      Select the Primary partition (Format it if it was used before) and click Next.'
    areaToImprove: OS installation - disk partitioning
    activityId: coc1-os-install
  - ruleName: Wrong installer image
    moduleId: COC1
    category: 
    keywords:
    - bootable usb
    - .iso
    - installer image
    whatWentWrong: That isn't the installer image the job needs.
    howToFix: Use the image named on the job order.
    correctProcedure: Check the job order for the operating system and edition required,
      then select exactly that ISO before writing the flash drive. Writing the wrong
      image wastes the drive and the customer's time.
    areaToImprove: Preparing installation media
    activityId: coc1-usb
  - ruleName: Rufus step
    moduleId: COC1
    category: 
    keywords:
    - rufus
    whatWentWrong: That Rufus step isn't right.
    howToFix: Official site first, then Device, Boot selection, START.
    correctProcedure: 'Download Rufus only from its official site (rufus.ie). In
      Rufus: Device = the USB flash drive; Boot selection = the Windows ISO from
      the job order; Partition scheme = GPT for UEFI (MBR for a legacy BIOS); keep
      the default file system; press START and confirm the warning that the drive
      will be erased.'
    areaToImprove: Preparing installation media
    activityId: coc1-usb
  - ruleName: Windows Setup choice
    moduleId: COC1
    category: 
    keywords:
    - os setup
    whatWentWrong: That isn't the option this job needs.
    howToFix: Re-read the job order and choose the matching option.
    correctProcedure: 'Read each Windows Setup screen: language and region, Install
      now, the edition on the job order, accept the licence, Custom: Install Windows
      only, then the partition you prepared.'
    areaToImprove: OS installation choices
    activityId: coc1-os-install
  - ruleName: Driver order
    moduleId: COC1
    category: 
    keywords:
    - installed out of order
    - must be installed first
    whatWentWrong: Drivers were installed in the wrong order.
    howToFix: Install the chipset (motherboard) driver first.
    correctProcedure: Install the chipset driver first so Windows identifies the
      other devices correctly, then the network, audio and display drivers. Restart
      when asked, then install the application software and Windows updates.
    areaToImprove: Driver and software installation
    activityId: coc1-system-config
  - ruleName: Patch panel termination
    moduleId: COC2
    category: 
    keywords:
    - termination
    - punch
    whatWentWrong: The patch panel termination isn't right.
    howToFix: Follow the panel's colour code and seat each wire fully.
    correctProcedure: Keep the jacket close to the panel and each pair twisted right
      up to the terminal. Lay each conductor in the slot shown by the panel's colour
      code (T568A or T568B as specified), then punch down with the tool's cutting
      blade facing the waste side. Test the port afterwards.
    areaToImprove: Structured cabling (punch-down)
    activityId: coc2-punchdown
  - ruleName: IP settings rejected
    moduleId: COC2
    category: 
    keywords:
    - configuration was rejected
    whatWentWrong: Those network settings won't work together.
    howToFix: Same network, same subnet mask, no duplicate addresses.
    correctProcedure: Give each device an address in the same network with the same
      subnet mask and no duplicates - for example 192.168.1.10 and 192.168.1.11 with
      255.255.255.0.
    areaToImprove: IP addressing
    activityId: coc2-connectivity
  - ruleName: Peer unreachable
    moduleId: COC2
    category: 
    keywords:
    - could not reach
    - connectivity
    whatWentWrong: The devices can't reach each other.
    howToFix: Check the cable and link lights, then each device's IP settings.
    correctProcedure: Check the physical link first (correct cable type, fully seated,
      link lights on), then the IP address and subnet mask on both ends, then test
      again with ping.
    areaToImprove: Testing connectivity
    activityId: coc2-connectivity
  - ruleName: Cable failed tester
    moduleId: COC2
    category: cable
    keywords: []
    whatWentWrong: The cable failed the tester.
    howToFix: Check the colour order at both ends against the standard.
    correctProcedure: 'T568B pin order: 1 white-orange, 2 orange, 3 white-green,
      4 blue, 5 white-blue, 6 green, 7 white-brown, 8 brown. T568A swaps the orange
      and green pairs (1 white-green, 2 green, 3 white-orange, 6 orange). Straight-through
      = the same standard at both ends; crossover = T568A at one end, T568B at the
      other. Untwist no more than 13 mm, push every conductor to the end of the plug,
      crimp once firmly, then test all 8 pins.'
    areaToImprove: Cable termination (T568A / T568B)
    activityId: coc2-crimping
  - ruleName: Server step out of sequence
    moduleId: COC3
    category: 
    keywords:
    - refused on
    whatWentWrong: That action doesn't belong at this point of the setup.
    howToFix: Check which part of the server setup comes next.
    correctProcedure: 'Server setup order: set the computer name and a static IP
      address; install the AD DS (and DNS) roles; promote the server to a domain
      controller; create OUs, users and groups; create the shared folders; set share
      and NTFS permissions; test from a client and complete the report.'
    areaToImprove: Server setup sequence
    activityId: coc3-server
  - ruleName: Server value wrong
    moduleId: COC3
    category: configuration
    keywords: []
    whatWentWrong: That value isn't what the job order specifies.
    howToFix: Check the value against the job order's specifications.
    correctProcedure: 'Enter each setting exactly as the job order specifies: computer
      name, static IP address, subnet mask, default gateway and preferred DNS server.
      A server needs its name and static address BEFORE roles are installed or it
      is promoted to a domain controller.'
    areaToImprove: Server configuration values
    activityId: coc3-server
  - ruleName: Ping failed
    moduleId: COC3
    category: connectivity
    keywords: []
    whatWentWrong: The ping test failed.
    howToFix: Check both machines with ipconfig, fix the address or mask, and ping
      again.
    correctProcedure: A ping fails when the hosts are on different subnets, have
      duplicate addresses, or have no working link. Check the settings on both machines
      with ipconfig, correct the address or subnet mask, then ping again.
    areaToImprove: Testing network services
    activityId: coc3-server
  - ruleName: Repair before diagnosis
    moduleId: 
    category: 
    keywords:
    - before diagnosing
    whatWentWrong: The repair started before the fault was diagnosed.
    howToFix: Observe and diagnose first, then repair.
    correctProcedure: 'Follow the troubleshooting process: 1) identify the problem;
      2) establish a probable cause; 3) test it; 4) plan and carry out the repair;
      5) verify the whole system works; 6) document the findings. Diagnose before
      you repair.'
    areaToImprove: Troubleshooting process
    activityId: coc4-tickets
  - ruleName: Wrong diagnosis
    moduleId: 
    category: diagnosis
    keywords: []
    whatWentWrong: That cause doesn't match the evidence.
    howToFix: Look again at what you observed.
    correctProcedure: 'Gather evidence before choosing a cause: power the machine
      on and observe (fans, beeps, lights, POST messages), then inspect inside for
      loose, missing or unseated parts and cables. Choose the cause that explains
      ALL the symptoms.'
    areaToImprove: Diagnosing from evidence
    activityId: coc4-tickets
  - ruleName: Repair not verified
    moduleId: 
    category: verification
    keywords: []
    whatWentWrong: The machine still fails after the repair.
    howToFix: Go back to diagnosis.
    correctProcedure: 'After a repair, power on and confirm the fault is gone: the
      machine passes POST, boots, and the reported problem no longer occurs. If it
      still fails, the diagnosis was incomplete - return to it.'
    areaToImprove: Verifying repairs
    activityId: coc4-tickets
  - ruleName: Ticket unresolved
    moduleId: 
    category: unresolved
    keywords: []
    whatWentWrong: The job was left unfinished.
    howToFix: 
    correctProcedure: 'See each ticket through: observe, diagnose, repair, verify,
      and record the cause before leaving the site.'
    areaToImprove: Completing each job
    activityId: coc4-tickets
  - ruleName: Cause not recorded
    moduleId: 
    category: identification
    keywords: []
    whatWentWrong: The cause was not recorded.
    howToFix: 
    correctProcedure: Record the diagnosed cause on the ticket as part of the job
      - a repair with no recorded cause is incomplete work and cannot be checked
      by the next technician.
    areaToImprove: Recording the cause
    activityId: coc4-tickets
  - ruleName: Time
    moduleId: 
    category: time
    keywords: []
    whatWentWrong: Time ran out.
    howToFix: 
    correctProcedure: Read the job order fully first, then work methodically. If
      a step takes too long, re-check the job order and the standard procedure rather
      than trying things at random.
    areaToImprove: Working within the time allowed
    activityId: 
  activities:
  - activityId: coc1-disassembly
    title: 'COC1 Story: Disassemble the system unit'
    moduleId: COC1
    sceneName: COC1
    whatToPractise: Practise the removal order and disconnecting cables safely.
  - activityId: coc1-assembly
    title: 'COC1 Story: Reassemble the system unit'
    moduleId: COC1
    sceneName: COC1
    whatToPractise: Seat the CPU and RAM correctly and reconnect every cable.
  - activityId: coc1-usb
    title: 'COC1 Story: Create the bootable USB'
    moduleId: COC1
    sceneName: COC1
    whatToPractise: Get Rufus from the official site and write the correct ISO.
  - activityId: coc1-os-install
    title: 'COC1 Story: Install Windows'
    moduleId: COC1
    sceneName: COC1
    whatToPractise: Prepare the partition and complete Windows Setup.
  - activityId: coc1-system-config
    title: 'COC1 Story: Drivers, software and updates'
    moduleId: COC1
    sceneName: COC1
    whatToPractise: Install drivers in order, then software and updates, then test
      and report.
  - activityId: coc2-crimping
    title: 'COC2 Story: Make and test UTP cables'
    moduleId: COC2
    sceneName: COC2-StoryMode
    whatToPractise: Build straight-through and crossover cables to T568A / T568B.
  - activityId: coc2-punchdown
    title: 'COC2 Story: Patch panel punch-down'
    moduleId: COC2
    sceneName: COC2-StoryMode
    whatToPractise: Terminate the patch panel to the colour code and test the port.
  - activityId: coc2-connectivity
    title: 'COC2 Story: Connect and test devices'
    moduleId: COC2
    sceneName: COC2-StoryMode
    whatToPractise: Set matching IP settings and prove the link with ping.
  - activityId: coc3-server
    title: 'COC3 Story: Configure the server'
    moduleId: COC3
    sceneName: COC3
    whatToPractise: Follow the setup order from static IP to shared folders and permissions.
  - activityId: coc4-tickets
    title: 'COC4 Story: Service tickets'
    moduleId: COC4
    sceneName: COC4-Hub
    whatToPractise: Observe, diagnose, repair, verify and record - one ticket at
      a time.
  outcomeLinks:
